# Nino - minimal Apache hardening defaults. Harmless if AllowOverride
# doesn't apply this file (eg. a PHP-FPM/nginx deployment) - see
# docs/setup.md's "Webserver (production)" for the equivalent nginx rules.

# Never serve a dotfile directly - matches the filename only (not the
# containing directory, so _editor/.cache/script.js is unaffected), which
# is exactly what's needed: _admin/.restore-key.php is a real dotfile, while
# content/.auth/ and content/.logs/ are dotdirs whose files inside
# (eg. 2026-01-01.php) aren't themselves dotfiles - those stay protected
# by their own self-exiting .php stub instead (see docs/developer.md's
# "Encryption / stub conventions").
<FilesMatch "^\.">
	Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# The project's own state (see \Nino\Filesystem::getContentPath()) is only
# ever read by php, never served - denied by content/.htaccess rather than
# from here, since a rule written here would have to name an absolute url
# path and would therefore miss a subdirectory install (/nino/dir). Both are
# belt and braces next to the 403 stub each of those files carries itself.

# Don't let a directory with no index.php list its contents - matters most
# for _editor/.backups-*/, whose only real protection is that its random
# directory name is never linked from anywhere
Options -Indexes